Harris, the neutral, male, human barbarian:
  Harris went genoless just because he never got a chance to genocide
anything, though by the castle I was excited and I doubt I would have
broken the conduct even if I had gotten the chance. That meant that I
had to fight L, h, and disenchanters; this was also a problem because I
was always weak in spells and ranged weapons; I fought almost every
single lich and mind flayer in melee, and used Elbereth (or abused if
you believe in that) to kill them. I was more concerned about liches
though; some early success with hit and run against MF, which was pure
luck; trying to replicate my success meant much lost knowledge. On my
ascension run, I had to explore almost every single level above my
stash as I went.

  Harris got lucky early on; exploring the gnomish mines yielded one
magic lamp from a store, plus two more from a double bones file, along
with gauntlets of dexterity and a cloak of magic resistance, all
cursed. The minetown alter was co-aligned, so I made holy water and
blessed most of this stuff, including two of the lamps, which I used to
wish for blessed +1 SDSM and an "amulet of life saveing;" the
misspelling earned me an amulet of ESP instead. I got the luckstone,
found a touchstone, blessed it and started collecting gems. I went a
bit overboard, and mined most of some levels. I bought some protection,
then went up and did sokoban, which had a BOH.
  Some time after this, I lost my cloak to a potion of polymorph, so I
blessed my last lamp and burned it for another cloak. I found the
Vorpal blade, and used it until I realized it wasn't fooprofed, which
was a bit of a turn-off, so I went back to my battle-axe. I found two
co-aligned alters on one level; one with a priest, and at this point I
had enough gold to buy some protection. I started sacrificing, in hopes
of getting a decent weapon, but I never got any good weapons until much
later.
  I did the quest, which seemed harder this time; as I did it, I felt
like I wasn't quite ready; maybe it was a lack of firepower, but I felt
like the trolls were giving me a hard time. I pressed it though, and
reached the bottom level. The one time before when I did the barbarian
quest I just hit Thoth Amon with wands until he died; this time he
teleported to me before I was expecting him, and I had to fight him,
following him up the stairs. I finally won, and took the bell and heart
with me.
  I went down a few levels, and found Medusa; I killed her went back to
nurse dance; I got grabbed by a giant eel and killed, but I had found a
AoLS somewhere, so I got a second chance to kill it with a WoD. I
descended until I saw the castle. I went back and looked for gold;
while digging out a vault, I found ludios. Cleared it, and took a WoD,
adding it to the one I had from the quest. I went in the back-door of
the castle; I've never been able to figure out how to open the
drawbridge, even with a suitable instrument, but it didn't matter. I
pressed the attack, preventing everyone from dropping through the
trapdoors like they did the first time I met the castle. The funny
thing is, right after clearing it, I realized that I had a ring of
conflict in my pack. It would have saved me some real trouble when I
had to deal with nasties. I got the /ow but didn't need anything, so I
saved it; I also got speed boots from the armory.
  I cleared the Valley of the Dead, but decided to wait before
Gehemmon. I saced more, and got Magicbane, which I kept for engraving.
I realized I had all of my holy water in my BOH, so I trekked up to the
mines and found a sack for some water and a blessed scroll of remove
curse. I fooproofed my armor and weapons, repairing the Vorpal blade in
the process. I twoweaponed it and a silver saber for the rest of the
game. I used a magic marker to enchant my armor significantly, and
wished for an AoLS. I gathered 20 or so !oHoly Water.
  I entered Gehemmon, and explored all of the first few levels, but got
tired and stopped doing that. I killed Asmodeus, Baalzebub, and
Juiblex, then found Vlad for the first time. I found him easy (YANI:
have all whole room open, so you've got to fight all the V's at once.)
and found orcustown, where my last good barbarian had died. I dug down
one level, then went down one more exploring, and caught my first
glimpse of the Wizard of Yendor. I was excited, but promptly fled back
up the stairs.
  I stopped to nurse dance between the Wizard and Orcus, then got a
nasty shock when a Master Lich tported right next to me. I had
teleportitis and a =oTC, so I jumped to the up-stairs, hoping to gain
time. No luck, so I burned Elbereth, then dressed, armed, and killed
the lich and his summoned hordes. I went up to Orcus, killed him and
took his wand, then dashed through orcustown; I didn't feel like
clearing it at the time. I went back to my alter and stash; I don't
remember what for. Went back, cleared Orcustown, found a much desired
magic lamp to replace the last one I burned, loitered above the wizard
while digging some paths, then went down.
  I found out that the Wizard wasn't going to jump out and kill me, and
I couldn't reach him, so I went down some more. I found the entrance,
and put on my WWBoots and oilskin cloak to deal with the kraken; then
opened up the tower and cleared the first level.
  I stopped and descended some more; I found the vibrating square and
marked it, then went back up to deal with the Wizard. I didn't have any
real problems until I opened up his block; then I realized in terror,
as he vaporized my cloak, that I was still wearing the oilskin cloak
and water walking boots, instead of my CoMR and Speed boots.
Fortunately, it was only my cloak, not my armor, so I popped the CoMR
on and led him over land, where I killed him with a WoD. I took the
book, then, having heard his corpse would give me teleport control, I
ate him. I took the penalties for cannibalism; whatever they were, they
were worth it. I descended.
  At this point I probably had about 400HP, ac-29, and a +7 Vorpal and
+6 silver s. I stopped trying to bless my !oFH or enhance my !oEH; I
just drank any of them that I found, leading to an endgame total of
447hp.
  Also at this point, much of my inventory was un-ided; I knew the key
things, but I had lost my knowledge of many other items to MFs. Here, I
did not write down my inventory, but if I could honestly remember what
something was, I would name it. This led to a funny thing when I
incorrectly named some forgotten wand wishing.
  At the vibrating square, I realized that I didn't know how to open
it; after summoning undead and in fear I would burn through charges on
the bell, I consulted spoilers. I did it properly this time, and
descended into the sanctum. I had a bit of trouble when I stripped
naked to deal with a disenchanter; Some other stuff showed up, and I
had to run to get dressed. I let conflict deal with him, and cleaned up
the mess. I entered the Inner Sanctum, praising the dev-team for making
priests summon things that were so weak and made such great barriers. I
started whacking the high priest, but I was being smitten by Moloch, so
I decided to burn a WoD charge instead. I took the amulet and ran. I
killed the Wizard a few times on my way up; always in melee. I ran into
some trouble in the swamp, when I ran into an arch-lich; I was far from
the stairs, couldn't teleport, and engraving Elbereth took several
steps; in the end I just sat there and waited for him to come to me;
then out-ran most of the hordes.
  I made it out of Gehemmon, stopped at ludios to grab about a dozen
k-rations, then headed up to the planes; as I said before, I had to
explore almost everything as I went. I got to DL1; I wished for an
amulet of magical breathing, since I didn't know what to expect on
water; I replaced my AoLS with it; I invoked the heart, and I went up.
  On Earth, I killed the wizard in melee; then cleared the first cell.
I was dissapointed when I realized I would need to dig my way out; I
had no way to locate the portals, so I figured I would just be running
around wildly. I took the wands of digging from the first cell, then
tried to pick-ax my way out. Right away an earth elemental showed up; I
took this to mean that all the walls would come to life when I tried to
dig them, so I killed him, took out my wands, and zapped myself to the
next cell. Lucky me; the portal is right there. But for some reason I
wouldn't go through. Maybe it's water or air, and I need to be
levitating or have magical breathing? I set myself up for those things,
but no luck. Perhaps it's the wrong portal? Maybe there are two? Ok,
next cell. I fought here, killed the wizard again, and headed back to
the portal to figure out what to do. Half way there, it hit me. Maybe
the wizard stole the amulet? I checked my inventory and saw that it was
true, so I paid his corpse a visit and retrieved the amulet. Then I
went through the portal to air.
  The plane of air gave me some trouble; as I said, I had no way to
find the portal. I also didn't feel like fighting everything on this
level; I put on my =oC and let the fight a bit, but they weren't dense
enough to kill themselves off. I wandered around aimlessly, trying to
hit the portal, but they started getting dense, and I was having to run
from MF's until they got killed. Eventual, I took out my WoW[0:0] and
got a last charge out of it; I wished for a crystal ball. I used it to
find the portal, and it worked well. Oh, and I the air elementals
didn't give me much trouble; I never dropped below 300hp at any time in
the end game.
  On fire, I wandered around a bit; it was nice to be back on solid
ground, for the most part, and I could fight mind flayers. I wasn't
able to find the portal with the crystal ball though; I think it must
have been out of charges. I gave up on that, and started wandering
methodically from one side to the other; eventually it paid off, and I
hit the portal.
  Water held one nice surprise; in the future, I'll know that I don't
need magical breathing. On the other hand, I didn't have my oilskin
cloak, so I kept the "oMB on for most of the time. Once again, I
wandered, and eventually, after getting board and reading spoilers, I
put on the Amulet of Yendor. I never felt it get hot, but I went over
to inspect some gem, and it turned out to be the portal.
  On Astral, I showed up levitating right next to an arch-lich; that
was unpleasant, but I had ground beneath me again, so I dropped down,
engraved Elbereth, put on my AoLS, and killed him. I headed to the
right wearing =oFA and =oC. It turned out to be famine; I killed him on
the second shot of my WoD. I fought my way through, killed him again
when he came back, and continued to the alter. Chaotic. I don't quite
remember the sequence, but I killed him twice more getting out, once in
melee. I'd been worried about him; my k-rations were starting to look
insuficent, but I was always able to kill him quickly enough that he
didn't give me trouble.
  I put on my blindfold, and saw death was in the middle. What the
hell, I'll try it. I killed him in melee in one round, and progressed
to the lawful altar. I turned around, waited while a priest and death
fought (the priest won) killed the priest, and continued out.
  On the left, pestilence. Once again, I don't quite remember the
sequence, but I hit him with a WoD and fought my way through to the
altar, where I offered the true Amulet of Yendor to Crom. Somehow I got
counted as killing pestilence twice.
  All total, I killed the Wizard of Yendor eight times, Death twice,
Famine four times,  and Pestilence twice. I never genocided anything,
and used seven wishes, though unfortunately I can't currently account
for all of them. I had four amulets of life saving, plus one other
which I had used, and only 3 of my 20+ potions of holy water left. I
was L24 with 447hp, and ascended with 7249084 points. As you probibly
see, I was rather spoiled, but not so much that I didn't learn some
things myself.



